Everphone GmbH, a Berlin-based startup founded in 2016, pioneered Device-as-a-Service (DaaS) for corporate smartphones and tablets, managing 400,000+ devices for 1,000+ companies including international consulting firms and DAX-listed corporations. Rather than ownership, enterprises rent devices with inclusive maintenance, replacement, and support services. Upon return, devices undergo comprehensive refurbishment and reenter the circulation cycle. The model achieves 95%+ device lifecycle extension, with only 5% entering recycling. This system generates predictable revenue, enables ESG compliance reporting, and eliminates customer capital expenditure while maintaining device availability and support—demonstrating viability of outcomes-oriented circular economy at enterprise scale.